# ${name}

A FastAPI service driven by a statechart, scaffolded by
`xsm new --template fastapi` from the
[`fastapi_orders` example](https://github.com/basiltt/xstate-statemachine/tree/main/examples/integrations/fastapi_orders).

| File | What it is |
|:--|:--|
| `machine.json` | The chart (id `${machine_id}`). Edit it in the Stately editor and re-export. |
| `models.py` | One Pydantic `EventModel` per event, plus the context model. |
| `logic.py` | Actions, guards and the (fake) payment service. |
| `app.py` | `StatechartRegistry` + `StatechartRouter` + `instrument_app`. |
| `tests/` | Plain pytest + `TestClient`. |

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
xsm validate --plain machine.json
python -m pytest tests -q
python app.py --role init                 # create the SQLite schema once
uvicorn app:app --workers 4               # the API, at /${name}/{id}
python app.py --role scheduler            # exactly one: wakes `after` timers
```

Set `XSM_REDIS_URL=redis://...` to switch from SQLite to Redis (install
`xstate-statemachine[fastapi,redis]`). See the integrations guide:
https://basiltt.github.io/xstate-statemachine/guide/integrations/
